    "https://www.rollins.edu/careers/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at Rollins Skip to main content Close Search For You Prospective Students Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Professional Advancement Graduate Studies Graduate Business Executive Education Current Students Parents & Families Alumni & Supporters Employers Media Resources MyRollins Library Wellness Center Careers at Rollins Campus Map Community Events Arts & Culture Bookstore Emergency Info Sports About Rollins News Working At Rollins Who We Are Faculty Development Grants & Sponsored Research Our Benefits Our Culture Our Location Our Service Excellence Job Openings All Job Openings Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Adjunct Jobs Student Jobs Required Notices Directions & Parking Payroll Search Toggle Menu Search Working At Rollins Back Who We Are Faculty Development Grants & Sponsored Research Our Benefits Our Culture Our Location Our Service Excellence Job Openings Back All Job Openings Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Adjunct Jobs Student Jobs Required Notices Directions & Parking Payroll For You Back Prospective Students Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Professional Advancement Graduate Studies Graduate Business Executive Education Current Students Parents & Families Alumni & Supporters Employers Media Resources Back MyRollins Library Wellness Center Careers at Rollins Campus Map Community Events Arts & Culture Bookstore Emergency Info Sports About Rollins News Careers at Rollins The Rollins Employee Experience Driven by purpose. Powered through people. At Rollins College, our greatest strength lies in our people, whoÂ deliver our award-winning success in academic excellence and service. We invite you to explore the opportunity to join our vibrant community and discover why so many passionate and talented individuals choose Rollins as their employer of choice. We are dedicated to fostering a welcoming, engaging, and thriving workplace where fairness, wellness, and the open exchange of diverse views, experiences, and ideas are not just valuesâthey define our culture and ensure that everyone is valued and belongs. Learn more about the Rollins culture Â and view available positions below. Careers at Rollins At Rollins, weâre committed to educating the next generation of global citizens and responsible leaders. Be a part of the Rollins experience and find a place where you belong. Ready to join us? Staff Job Openings Full-Time, Part-Time, and Temporary Staff The moment you first set foot on campus, you'll feel an energy, a purpose, and a passion for learning. Then, you'll discover why so people have made Rollins College their employer of choice. Faculty Job Openings Tenure Track and Non-Tenure Track Faculty Rollins' faculty are dedicated to academic excellence, global citizenship, and lifelong learning. Our focus on small, discussion-style classes allows faculty to engage students through personalized learning experiences. Adjunct Faculty Job Openings Adjunct Faculty We accept applications to fill current and future part-time, temporary teaching positions in multiple disciplines. Applicants will be contacted on an as-needed basis. Student Job Openings Student On-Campus Employment Whether itâs managing social media content for the Collegeâs Office of Marketing or running the box office at the Annie Russell Theatre, on-campus student employment opportunities at Rollins yield big results. Rollins College is an equal-opportunityÂ institution. Rollins does not discriminate on the basis of sex, disability, race, age, religion, color, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, physical characteristics, or any other category protected by College policy or federal, state, or local law for employment and in our educational programs and activities.Â We will provide reasonable accommodations for employees and job applicants to search for a job opening and fully participate in all aspects of the recruitment process, consistent with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and our Â Accessibility Statement . Any applicant who requires reasonable accommodations for any part of the application or hiring process may contact us by phone at 407.646.2102 or in writing at Â humanresources@rollins.edu . We're Much More than a Beautiful Campus Explore America's Most Beautiful Campus Itâs easy to see why Rollins is considered one of Americaâs most beautiful college campuses. Thereâs a lot to loveâfrom the shimmering waters of Lake Virginia to the palm trees and the brick pathways. Zoom in though, and you'll discover that our campus is beautiful for dozens of reasons beyond its stunning lakeside location and sunny weather. What's Happening at Rollins Students, faculty and staff shine brighter at Rollins. See what's new. September 12, 2023 Rollins Named a 2023 âGreat College to Work Forâ For the 15th consecutive year, The Chronicle of Higher Education has named Rollins a âGreat College to Work For.â Rollins Named a 2023 âGreat College to Work Forâ July 06, 2023 Rollins Receives Scientific Equipment Grant The Sherman Fairchild Foundation has awarded Rollins a grant that will enhance learning in the sciences and make biology and chemistry majors even more competitive for careers in STEM. Rollins Receives Scientific Equipment Grant May 25, 2023 4 Rollins Students Earn Fulbright Scholarships Four Tars have received the distinguished Fulbright Scholarship, including two teaching assignments and two awards to pursue graduate school and research opportunities. 4 Rollins Students Earn Fulbright Scholarships Contact Us Human Resources, Payroll & Risk Management at Rollins humanresources@rollins.edu | 407.646.2102 Start Exploring Virtual Campus Tour From our discussion-based classes to our brand-new applied learning center, navigate nearly 20 campus locations through interactive 360-degree photography and immersive video. 1000 Holt Ave. Winter Park, FL 32789 Phone: 407.646.2000 Campus Map & Directions ADMISSION INFORMATION Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Professional Advancement Graduate Studies Graduate Business Executive Education INFORMATION FOR Faculty & Staff Current Students Alumni & Supporters Parents & Families RESOURCES Library MyRollins Registrar Campus Map Events Calendar Rollins News Emergency Info INFORMATION ABOUT Rollins Sports Giving Arts & Culture Rollins Careers Bookstore For the Media EASE Grant Performance Measures Facebook Instagram YouTube TikTok LinkedIn Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Accessibility Statement Title IX Policies & Resources Nondiscrimination Policy © 2026 Rollins College"
