    "https://www.rollins.edu/careers/our-culture/": {
      "title": "Our Culture & Values",
      "description": "Our Culture Skip to main content Close Search For You Prospective Students Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Professional Advancement Graduate Studies Graduate Business Executive Education Current Students Parents & Families Alumni & Supporters Employers Media Resources MyRollins Library Wellness Center Careers at Rollins Campus Map Community Events Arts & Culture Bookstore Emergency Info Sports About Rollins News Working At Rollins Who We Are Faculty Development Grants & Sponsored Research Our Benefits Our Culture Our Location Our Service Excellence Job Openings All Job Openings Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Adjunct Jobs Student Jobs Required Notices Directions & Parking Payroll Search Toggle Menu Search Working At Rollins Back Who We Are Faculty Development Grants & Sponsored Research Our Benefits Our Culture Our Location Our Service Excellence Job Openings Back All Job Openings Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Adjunct Jobs Student Jobs Required Notices Directions & Parking Payroll For You Back Prospective Students Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Professional Advancement Graduate Studies Graduate Business Executive Education Current Students Parents & Families Alumni & Supporters Employers Media Resources Back MyRollins Library Wellness Center Careers at Rollins Campus Map Community Events Arts & Culture Bookstore Emergency Info Sports About Rollins News Working at Rollins Our Culture & Values The Perfect Balance At Rollins, we believe that our institution and students flourish when our workforce thrives. We are committed to creating a supportive and inclusive environment for all employees while upholding the standards of excellence that define our daily service. From offering flexible work schedules and comprehensive well-being programs to fostering employee resource groups and recognition initiatives, we understand that a healthy work/life balance is essential to the Rollins culture. Your well-being is our priority, and we are here to support you every step of the way. An Award-Winning Environment Rollins is frequently recognized for everything from compensation and benefits to career development programs and job satisfaction. 15 X Consecutively named a Great College to Work For â The Chronicle of Higher Education Up to 11.5 % in retirement contributions from Rollins for full time faculty and staff No. 7 Best Health Services â The Princeton Review, 2027 No. 2 Best City to Start a Career in the U.S. â Wallet Hub Awards & Rankings August 19, 2026 The Princeton Review Recognizes Rollins Among Nationâs Best Colleges Rollins has been ranked one of the nationâs best 392 colleges by The Princeton Review and has landed among the top 25 in 11 additional categories. The Princeton Review Recognizes Rollins Among Nationâs Best Colleges May 21, 2026 Gary â26 Earns Fulbright Scholarship Biology and environmental studies double major Makenna Morrison Gary â26 has earned a 2026â27 Fulbright Study/Research Award to study biodiversity at National Taiwan University. Gary â26 Earns Fulbright Scholarship April 28, 2026 Rollins Announces 2026 Student Achievement Awards The College recognized 35 students for their academic achievements and positive contributions to campus and the community at the 2026 Student Awards Banquet. Rollins Announces 2026 Student Achievement Awards Everyone Belongs Curious about our core principles and dedication to celebrating, uplifting, and recognizing every member of our vibrant campus community? Rollins is committed to fostering strong, thriving communities for all. Learn More Our Service Excellence Rollinsâ Service Excellence Initiative strives to improve how we treat our students, visitors to our campus, and our colleagues. Responsive, respectful, inclusive, competent, and collaborative are the five standards that drive this level of service for every employee. Learn More Employee Resource Groups Rollinsâ Employee Resource Group (ERG) Program is a strategic pillar in fostering a thriving workplace where innovation and employee engagement are valued and where everyone feels connected, appreciated, and supported. Open to all faculty and staff, each of Rollinsâ ERGs is a network of employees who voluntarily come together to provide support and create connections based on shared interests, experiences, and/or identities. Learn More 1000 Holt Ave. Winter Park, FL 32789 Phone: 407.646.2000 Campus Map & Directions ADMISSION INFORMATION Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Professional Advancement Graduate Studies Graduate Business Executive Education INFORMATION FOR Faculty & Staff Current Students Alumni & Supporters Parents & Families RESOURCES Library MyRollins Registrar Campus Map Events Calendar Rollins News Emergency Info INFORMATION ABOUT Rollins Sports Giving Arts & Culture Rollins Careers Bookstore For the Media EASE Grant Performance Measures Facebook Instagram YouTube TikTok LinkedIn Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Accessibility Statement Title IX Policies & Resources Nondiscrimination Policy © 2026 Rollins College"
    },
