      "description": "Location & Region Skip to main content Close Search For You Prospective Students Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Professional Advancement Graduate Studies Graduate Business Executive Education Current Students Parents & Families Alumni & Supporters Employers Media Resources MyRollins Library Wellness Center Careers at Rollins Campus Map Community Events Arts & Culture Bookstore Emergency Info Sports About Rollins News Working At Rollins Who We Are Faculty Development Grants & Sponsored Research Our Benefits Our Culture Our Location Our Service Excellence Job Openings All Job Openings Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Adjunct Jobs Student Jobs Required Notices Directions & Parking Payroll Search Toggle Menu Search Working At Rollins Back Who We Are Faculty Development Grants & Sponsored Research Our Benefits Our Culture Our Location Our Service Excellence Job Openings Back All Job Openings Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Adjunct Jobs Student Jobs Required Notices Directions & Parking Payroll For You Back Prospective Students Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Professional Advancement Graduate Studies Graduate Business Executive Education Current Students Parents & Families Alumni & Supporters Employers Media Resources Back MyRollins Library Wellness Center Careers at Rollins Campus Map Community Events Arts & Culture Bookstore Emergency Info Sports About Rollins News Location & Region Rollins' home in Winter Park, Florida, will place you at an exciting crossroads of culture, commerce, professional opportunity, and fun. An afternoonâs walk along Park Avenueâjust steps away from campusâwill expose you to a few of the exciting cultural and recreational outlets you will enjoy as a member of the Rollins community. Winter Park Some of Winter Park's most popular attractions include... Festivals: Autumn Art Festival, Family Fall Festival, Florida Film Festival, Unity Heritage Festival, and Winter Park Sidewalk Art Festival Parks: Cady Way Park, Central Park, Dinky Dock Park, Kraft Azalea Gardens, Lake Island Park, Mead Garden, Phelps Park, Shady Park, and Ward Park Museums: Albin Polasek Museum and Sculpture Gardens, Rollins Museum of Art, Charles Hosmer Morse Museum of American Art, and Winter Park Historical Association & Museum Theaters: Annie Russell Theatre, Enzian Theater, Fred Stone Theatre, Paper Moon Theatre Company, and Winter Park Playhouse Sports & Recreation: Winter Park Golf Course, Winter Park Farmersâ Market, Lake Island Recreation Center, Winter Park Tennis Center, Scenic Boat Tours, and Winter Pines Golf Course Learn More Orlando Less than ten minutes away from the Rollins campus, Orlando continues to thrive as one of Americaâs fastest-growing metropolitan areas. With a population of more than 1.6 million, Orlando will offer you easy access toâ¦ Six zoos and wildlife refuges 52 million square feet of retail shopping space More than 5,000 restaurants More than 2,000 lakes, springs, and rivers Walt Disney World Orlando City Soccer Club of Major League Soccer The Orlando Philharmonic Orchestra And more... Your Guide to Living in Orlando A recent report by WalletHub ranked Orlando as the No. 1 midsize college city and the No. 2 city to start a career in the U.S. See What's Here 1000 Holt Ave. Winter Park, FL 32789 Phone: 407.646.2000 Campus Map & Directions ADMISSION INFORMATION Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Professional Advancement Graduate Studies Graduate Business Executive Education INFORMATION FOR Faculty & Staff Current Students Alumni & Supporters Parents & Families RESOURCES Library MyRollins Registrar Campus Map Events Calendar Rollins News Emergency Info INFORMATION ABOUT Rollins Sports Giving Arts & Culture Rollins Careers Bookstore For the Media EASE Grant Performance Measures Facebook Instagram YouTube TikTok LinkedIn Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Accessibility Statement Title IX Policies & Resources Nondiscrimination Policy © 2026 Rollins College"
