    "https://jobs.rollins.edu/jobs/associate-full-professor-operations-management-supply-chain-management-orlando-florida-united-states-winter-park-fl": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor, Operations Management & Supply Chain Management",
      "description": "Associate/Full Professor, Operations Management & Supply Chain Management - Winter Park, FL, Florida, United States Skip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\". Home Benefits Culture Location Service Excellence Job Openings All Job Openings Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Adjunct Jobs Student Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Associate/Full Professor, Operations Management & Supply Chain Management Winter Park, FL, Florida Crummer Graduate School of Business Faculty (Tenure-Track) Opening on: Aug 31 2026 Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary: The Crummer Graduate School of Business at Rollins College invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Associate or Full Professor in the area of operations and supply chain management beginning in August 2027. We are seeking a seasoned educator and thought leader who combines a strong academic foundation with a passion for shaping practice-oriented insights for today’s business leaders. We are seeking a seasoned educator and thought leader who combines a strong academic foundation with a passion for shaping practice-oriented insights for today’s business leaders. This is not a traditional operations management role. We are looking for someone who brings a systems thinking perspective to operations that emphasizes helping leaders understand how operational choices create second- and third-order effects across interconnected value chains and organizations. We are particularly interested in candidates exploring technology’s evolving role in operations ranging from business analytics and automation to AI-enabled decision-making, including how large language models and domain-specific AI shape operational resilience and performance. While this position emphasizes practical impact and executive education, we remain an AACSB-accredited institution with high standards for research productivity. Candidates must have a distinguished record of publishing in peer-reviewed academic journals as well as demonstrated excellence in teaching. However, this role is ideal for a scholar who has excelled in traditional academic research and MBA teaching and is now seeking to broaden their focus toward executive education, applied research, and practitioner-oriented thought leadership. We especially welcome candidates who: Have published in respected peer-reviewed journals and built a strong scholarly reputation, but also seek to translate those insights into frameworks, tools, and programs that impact practicing managers and executives. Can connect systems thinking and foresight to operational strategy, helping organizations navigate uncertainty, interconnected risks, and emerging technologies. Have experience engaging with business leaders or industry forums and can design executive education offerings that elevate Crummer’s presence in practice-oriented learning. Are collaborative and thrive in Crummer’s interdisciplinary, small-school environment, which emphasizes applied learning, close student-faculty engagement, and strong industry connections. Rollins College is a comprehensive liberal arts college located just north of Orlando, FL, a diverse metropolitan community with a thriving economic and cultural scene. Nearby Orlando International Airport provides easy access to U.S. and international destinations. The college emphasizes innovative and quality teaching in small classes and ranks number one among 121 Southern master’s-level universities in the annual rankings of “America’s Best Colleges,” released by U.S. News & World Report. Please visit the college website at www.rollins.edu . Minimum Qualifications and Education: Ph.D. from a full-time doctoral program with specialization in operations management, supply chain management, industrial engineering, or a closely related field from an AACSB, ABET, or EQUIS-accredited institution. Demonstrated record of publishing in peer-reviewed academic journals. Demonstrated excellence in teaching. Preferred Qualifications: Professional certifications (e.g., CPIM, PMP) or industry experience. Experience with operations management and design methods such as quality function deployment (QFD) and/or design thinking. Instructions to Applicants: Interested applicants must apply online via the College's employment website and upload the following materials as follows: Letter of interest Curriculum vita Contact information for three references on application **Review of applications will begin immediately until position is filled.* Inquiries can be directed to: Keenan Yoho Chair – Search Committee, Crummer Graduate School of Business kyoho@rollins.edu Benefits & Perks: Paid Holidays and College Closure Days Eligible for Medical, Prescription, Dental & Vision Insurances (within 30 days of hire) 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account ($125+/month) 100% Employer-Paid Short & Long Term Disability Insurance Domestic Partner Benefits 11.5% Employer Retirement Contributions Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Free On-Campus Parking Free Access to Campus Amenities (gyms, pools, library, sporting events and more) Free Full Tuition for Employees and their Families Pet Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program Flexible Spending Accounts Award-Winning Wellbeing Programs Plus More! Additional Perks: Rollins College is conveniently located on multiple Lynx Bus Routes (Winter Park/Rosemont-9 & Winter Park/Springs Village-23) and within walking distance from the Winter Park SunRail Station Local & National Discount Programs, including Winter Park Locations (i.e. shops, restaurants, gift cards, and more) Free E-Training Courses & Professional Development Opportunities IT Software & Laptop Discounts (Apple, Lenovo, and more) College Bookstore Discounts Annual Service Awards & Recognition Programs Discover what it's like to live in Orlando: Live, Work, Play and Learn Plus More! Click here to review our full benefits package! Equal Employment Opportunity: Rollins College is an equal opportunity institution. Rollins does not discriminate on the basis of sex, disability, race, age, religion, color, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, physical characteristics, or any other category protected by College policy or federal, state, or local law for employment and in our educational programs and activities. To learn more about our commitments, visit click here . Any applicant who requires reasonable accommodations for any part of the application or hiring process may contact us by phone or in writing to humanresources@rollins.edu | 407.646.2102. Employment Eligibility: All new employees must be eligible and show employment eligibility verification by the first date of employment at Rollins College, as legally required (e.g., Form I-9).  Rollins College will require proof of authorization to work in the United States. Further, based on the September 19, 2025, Presidential Proclamation and accompanying guidance from the USCIS and Department of State, the College may not be able to offer H-1B sponsorship. Particularly the College is not able to pay the fee accompanying new H-1B visa petitions. FLSA Status: Exempt Service Months: 9 Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! First Name (required) 6240ccb8 Last Name (required) 07823ef3 Email (required) e8bd6184 Job Alert 54b2311b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Crummer Graduate School Crummer Graduate School Employment Type Faculty (Tenure-Track) Faculty (Tenure-Track) Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Why Join Rollins? At Rollins College, we believe people thrive when they feel supported. Join a community that values flexibility, wellness, inclusion, and recognition. When our employees thrive, so do our students and our campus community! Total Rewards Rollins offers a variety of benefits for full-time and part-time roles: Generous Paid Time Off & Holidays Medical, Dental, Vision Insurances Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Employer Retirement Contributions Free Tuition for Employees & Families Domestic Partner Benefits Employee Assistance Program Pet Insurance Click here to learn more! Thriving Together Inclusive, mission-driven campus culture . Service Excellence : Delivering the Rollins experience is a shared responsibility Employee Resource Groups (ERGs) Chart Your Journey Here at Rollins. Minutes from Orlando, Steps Away From Endless Opportunities Located in Winter Park, Florida, (and just minutes away from Orlando), Rollins is perfectly positioned at the center of theme park adventures, thriving tech companies, and one of the nation’s most thriving job markets. Take a walk to award-winning dining on Park Ave. Hop on a 15-minute train ride to downtown Orlando’s growing arts scene and pro sports. Or sink your toes into the sand of one of the world's best beaches. Discover #ThisisOrlando! Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 4746f434 Last Name (required) 3ed060f0 Email (required) 93f36bb1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1000 Holt Ave. Winter Park, FL 32789 Phone: 407.646.2000 Campus Map & Directions ADMISSION INFORMATION Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Graduate Business and Executive Education Professional Advancement Graduate Studies INFORMATION FOR Faculty & Staff Current Students Alumni & Supporters Parents & Families RESOURCES Library MyRollins Registrar Campus Map Events Calendar Rollins News Emergency Info INFORMATION ABOUT Rollins Sports Giving Arts & Culture Rollins Careers Bookstore For the Media EASE Grant Performance Measures Privacy Policy | Terms and Conditions | Accessibility Statement | Title IX Policies & Resources | Nondiscrimination Policy © 2026 Rollins College Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s) Opens in new window PDF Download Word Download Excel Download PowerPoint Download Document Download Explore your accessibility options"
    },
    "https://jobs.rollins.edu/jobs/associate-full-professor-finance-orlando-florida-united-states-winter-park-fl": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor – Finance",
      "description": "Associate/Full Professor – Finance - Winter Park, FL, Florida, United States Skip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\". Home Benefits Culture Location Service Excellence Job Openings All Job Openings Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Adjunct Jobs Student Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Associate/Full Professor – Finance Winter Park, FL, Florida Business Crummer Graduate School of Business Faculty (Tenure-Track) Opening on: Aug 24 2026 Academic Affairs Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary: The Crummer Graduate School of Business at Rollins College in Winter Park, Florida offers a unique opportunity to qualified applicants with expertise in corporate finance and/or investments. If you share our passion for outstanding teaching, consider joining our faculty as an Associate/Full Professor of Finance in Fall 2027. Applicants should have a Ph.D. in Finance from an AACSB-accredited school. A professional certification (i.e., CFA) is desirable. We hire experienced faculty, many of whom have won teaching awards before joining Crummer. If you enjoy teaching and aspire to expand your teaching skills, this is the position for you. A successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching MBA students in both traditional and blended formats and have at least four years of teaching experience at an AACSB-accredited school. At Crummer, you will have the opportunity to teach students with varying ages and levels of experience, ranging from recent college graduates to senior executives. Our students demand much of us; they challenge and stimulate us as much as we do them. Crummer faculty are all dedicated to providing our students with an integrated, experiential educational environment. As a result, we have tremendous collaboration among the various disciplines. We are nimble and operate with little bureaucracy. All new Crummer faculty come without tenure and have three to four years to qualify for tenure based on teaching, research, and service. Teaching: To be successful at Crummer, you must be dedicated to great teaching. Crummer School faculty members take great pride in their teaching. We attract outstanding students who are motivated, eager to learn, and deeply engaged in our programs. We are looking for faculty who have already won teaching awards, especially at the MBA level. Fifty percent of your annual performance at Crummer will come from your teaching, as evaluated by colleagues and students. Finance faculty must teach the core finance course in the MBA program, as well as electives that match their background. Crummer faculty are encouraged to develop elective courses that bring their research interests and professional experiences into the classroom. Research: The Crummer faculty recognize that a broad range of research contributes to management practice. Thirty percent of your annual performance evaluation will come from your research at Crummer. Our faculty handbook spells out the exact requirements. Service: Crummer has 18 faculty members who collaborate between and among various disciplines. The remaining twenty percent of your annual performance evaluation is based on your service activities. We practice faculty governance without rancor and most of our decisions are unanimous. You will find collegiality one of the best parts of life at Crummer. Because we are unique, the Crummer School is not for everyone. If you are just starting your academic career, Crummer is not for you. If teaching is your primary motivation, you will likely find a good fit at Crummer. We are looking for a candidate who has already made a significant mark in research and is ready to transition to a program that truly does emphasize teaching. We also value practical professional experience as well as prior engagements with executives through teaching and/or consulting. Crummer is a great place to work—great students, wonderful colleagues, and a stimulating intellectual climate. We are an AACSB accredited, nationally ranked MBA-only graduate business school attached to a highly ranked undergraduate liberal arts college. Rollins College is a comprehensive liberal arts college located just north of Orlando, FL, a diverse metropolitan community with a thriving economic and cultural scene. Nearby Orlando International Airport provides easy access to U.S. and international destinations. The college emphasizes innovative and quality teaching in small classes and ranks number one among 121 Southern master’s-level universities in the annual rankings of “America’s Best Colleges,” released by U.S. News & World Report. Please visit the college website at www.rollins.edu . Minimum Qualifications and Education: Ph.D. in Finance from an AACSB-accredited school Demonstrated excellence in teaching graduate level finance courses Demonstrated record of publications to meet faculty qualifications as a scholarly academic Evidence of active research stream within finance Preferred Qualifications: Professional certifications (e.g., CFA) or industry experience Instructions to Applicants: Interested applicants must apply online via the College's employment website and upload the following materials as follows: Letter of interest Curriculum vita Evidence of sustained teaching excellence (such as teaching evaluations) in graduate finance courses Contact information for three references on application **Review of applications will begin immediately until the position is closed. Preference will be given to applications received by November 15, 2026. The appointment is expected to begin in September 2027.* Inquiries can be directed to: Dr. Koray D. Simsek, CFA Orchid/Singleton Chair and Professor of Finance Email: ksimsek@rollins.edu Benefits & Perks: Paid Holidays and College Closure Days Eligible for Medical, Prescription, Dental & Vision Insurances (within 30 days of hire) 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account ($125+/month) 100% Employer-Paid Short & Long Term Disability Insurance Domestic Partner Benefits 11.5% Employer Retirement Contributions Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Free On-Campus Parking Free Access to Campus Amenities (gyms, pools, library, sporting events and more) Free Full Tuition for Employees and their Families Pet Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program Flexible Spending Accounts Award-Winning Wellbeing Programs Plus More! Additional Perks: Rollins College is conveniently located on multiple Lynx Bus Routes (Winter Park/Rosemont-9 &  Winter Park/Springs Village-23) and within walking distance from the Winter Park SunRail Station Local & National Discount Programs, including Winter Park Locations (i.e. shops, restaurants, gift cards, and more) Free E-Training Courses & Professional Development Opportunities IT Software & Laptop Discounts (Apple, Lenovo, and more) College Bookstore Discounts Annual Service Awards & Recognition Programs Discover what it's like to live in Orlando: Live, Work, Play and Learn Plus More! Click here to review our full benefits package! Equal Employment Opportunity: Rollins College is an equal opportunity institution. Rollins does not discriminate on the basis of sex, disability, race, age, religion, color, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, physical characteristics, or any other category protected by College policy or federal, state, or local law for employment and in our educational programs and activities. To learn more about our commitments, visit click here . Any applicant who requires reasonable accommodations for any part of the application or hiring process may contact us by phone or in writing to humanresources@rollins.edu | 407.646.2102. Employment Eligibility: All new employees must be eligible and show employment eligibility verification by the first date of employment at Rollins College, as legally required (e.g., Form I-9).  Rollins College will require proof of authorization to work in the United States. Further, based on the September 19, 2025, Presidential Proclamation and accompanying guidance from the USCIS and Department of State, the College may not be able to offer H-1B sponsorship. Particularly the College is not able to pay the fee accompanying new H-1B visa petitions. FLSA Status: Exempt Service Months: 9 Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! First Name (required) ecaf04ac Last Name (required) caddb6cb Email (required) 787344d5 Job Alert 10edf7e1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Crummer Graduate School Crummer Graduate School Employment Type Faculty (Tenure-Track) Faculty (Tenure-Track) Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Why Join Rollins? At Rollins College, we believe people thrive when they feel supported. Join a community that values flexibility, wellness, inclusion, and recognition. When our employees thrive, so do our students and our campus community! Total Rewards Rollins offers a variety of benefits for full-time and part-time roles: Generous Paid Time Off & Holidays Medical, Dental, Vision Insurances Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Employer Retirement Contributions Free Tuition for Employees & Families Domestic Partner Benefits Employee Assistance Program Pet Insurance Click here to learn more! Thriving Together Inclusive, mission-driven campus culture . Service Excellence : Delivering the Rollins experience is a shared responsibility Employee Resource Groups (ERGs) Chart Your Journey Here at Rollins. Minutes from Orlando, Steps Away From Endless Opportunities Located in Winter Park, Florida, (and just minutes away from Orlando), Rollins is perfectly positioned at the center of theme park adventures, thriving tech companies, and one of the nation’s most thriving job markets. Take a walk to award-winning dining on Park Ave. Hop on a 15-minute train ride to downtown Orlando’s growing arts scene and pro sports. Or sink your toes into the sand of one of the world's best beaches. Discover #ThisisOrlando! Ready to Apply? First Name (required) bdfb01d2 Last Name (required) bf26910b Email (required) 3193bf4c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 1000 Holt Ave. Winter Park, FL 32789 Phone: 407.646.2000 Campus Map & Directions ADMISSION INFORMATION Full-Time Undergraduate Transferring to Rollins Graduate Business and Executive Education Professional Advancement Graduate Studies INFORMATION FOR Faculty & Staff Current Students Alumni & Supporters Parents & Families RESOURCES Library MyRollins Registrar Campus Map Events Calendar Rollins News Emergency Info INFORMATION ABOUT Rollins Sports Giving Arts & Culture Rollins Careers Bookstore For the Media EASE Grant Performance Measures Privacy Policy | Terms and Conditions | Accessibility Statement | Title IX Policies & Resources | Nondiscrimination Policy © 2026 Rollins College Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s) Opens in new window PDF Download Word Download Excel Download PowerPoint Download Document Download Explore your accessibility options"
